backport: title/author/subject metadata for html and fb2 (bug 709574)

BACKPORT of upstream mupdf 976c9f122e31f48e4b7f4dfd44a0b2703902085a, not a
change of ours. Drop it when the vendored mupdf moves past that commit - it is
on mupdf master but not in 1.28.2.

https://bugs.ghostscript.com/show_bug.cgi?id=709574

This is our own patch, upstreamed: the commit says "Based on a patch from
Krzysztof Kowalczyk of SumatraPDF", and it took our append_xml_text() /
collect_text() helpers verbatim. It replaces our
0015-html-fb2-author-and-annotation.

Upstream generalised it rather than bolting author/subject onto fz_html: the
parser now fills an fz_html_metadata { title, author, subject } instead of a
lone char **rtitle, and html title extraction goes through the same
text-gathering helpers, which is a little more resilient than reading a single
text node. Same three properties reach Document Properties as before.
---
